Reflection - Visualization Tool    Challenge    My question is : How do we spur rapid growth for a new line of digital products for organizations?    I work for a Montreal digital agency with 52 employees.  I was recently appointed to create a sales  presentation regardinga new product line we have developed. I wanted the sales representatives to  align their outlooks, to find how we should present these new products to potential customers and more  importantly, I wanted us as a team, to understand why and whenthese potential customers really need  these products.    Selection    I decided to use the Visualization Tool to create a diagram of our customers’ journey and build  personas before building the content and the tools our digital experts will be using to sell and promote  our solutions.  I chose this approach to better understand our users’ needs who are CMO’s, Marketing  directors and Brand managers and to build personas, identify patterns and find new innovative ways of  pitching to them.    Application    I started the process by designing a simple representation of our product line on a wall in the  conference room and designing a straw man on the opposite wall to represent a potential customer.  For the activity, I had installed easyflip sheets everywhere in the conference room so every stakeholder  could write directly on the walls.    Easyflip sheets

I divided the stakeholders into 2 groups of 2-3 participants each working on a wall to add symbols,  colors, diagrams and drawings to represent How they viewed our product line and our potential  customers.  I gave them a 60 minute period to discuss amongst themselves and to design what they  wanted on their respective walls.  Following this, I gave them 3 tasks to perform :

1. Pitch your work to the other group ;

2. Ask them what is missing to make their graphic representations more accurate ;

3. Find some patterns and synthesize them.

